Louise wants to borrow as much as possible to buy a car and she wants to repay the loan over four years.

Her bank offers loans at 6% per annum compounded monthly.

Louise plans to make the following repayments on the loan account.

\begin{itemize}
\item She will pay \$500 at the end of each month for the first two years.
\item She will increase this to \$800 at the end of each month for the next two years.
\end{itemize}

Present value interest factors for an annuity of \$1 for various interest rates ($r$) and periods of time ($N$) are given in the table below.

\extable{308_q38_t1}

Calculate the maximum amount that Louise would be able to borrow.
